    18	
    19	## Adversarial finding (one paragraph)
    20	
    21	S53's argument 2 — "diagonalisation costs O(K³) and is the dominant
    22	kernel-independent cost" — was framed as **per-query** cost. Under
    23	amortisation (compute the operator's spectrum once, serve many π(x)
    24	queries), the per-query cost reduces to the K-term explicit-formula
    25	sum, O(K). The setup K³ is paid once. **However**, Galway 2004 +
    26	Hiary computes the same K zeros at setup cost O(K^{17/13}) and
    27	serves the same per-query cost O(K). Both routes are subject to the
    28	identical K(x) ≈ √x worst-case requirement (Riemann-von Mangoldt /
    29	explicit-formula floor). The Connes route is therefore **strictly
    30	dominated by Galway** in every cost regime — by a factor of K^{22/13}
