    806	| S190 commit-thread step 5 (FINAL) — synthesis + thread DONE: chi_P MPS spectrum compiles into `π(N) = 0.21·π(N) [PNT-in-AP at sqf q ≤ N^{0.185}] + 0.79·π(N) [GUE-bulk MP]`, sharper closure of polylog spectral attack family | SYNTHESIS+CLOSURE | C | Commit-thread session 5/5 (final synthesis slot) on the S82 invariant-subspace theorem. **Compiled theorem (S190)**: combining S148 (refutation of S82's |L(1,χ)|² eigenvalue claim + Gallagher-variance K-formula), S166 (exact V_p ⊕ V_{2p}^prim energy via Ramanujan sums), S168 (squarefree extension to all sqf q with closed form `μ²(q)/φ(q)·(π(N)−r)²/N + R`), and S169 (empirical 21% spike-block-fraction at d=14,18,20 within 7%/5%/5%, finite-N Q_eff exponent ≈ 0.185), the chi_P MPS column-Gram operator decomposes additively into: (1) rank-1 wheel mean (excluded), (2) spike sector ≅ ⊕_{sqf q ≤ Q*≈N^{0.185}} V_q^prim carrying ≈ 0.21·π(N) energy, (3) bulk MP sector with σ-edge 2√(M·p·(1−p)) (M=√N, p=π(N)/N) carrying ≈ 0.79·π(N) energy. The spike eigenvectors ARE Dirichlet character vectors (S82 stands); the eigenvalues are Ramanujan-sum / principal-Dirichlet structure (NOT |L(1,χ)|², S148/S166). **Polylog-blocker reformulation (NEW for S190)**: computing π(N) ≡ computing the bulk MP sector at additive resolution q ≥ N^{0.185}; the spike sector reduces to PNT-in-AP at sqf q ≤ N^{0.185} computable in O(N^{0.185+ε}) by direct Fourier sieving but NOT polylog (E1.5 anchor); the bulk sector is GUE-pseudorandom across 35+ measures (S74/E1.5/T6 anchor). Both sub-sectors blocked. **Net effect**: structural progress, no algorithmic opening. The closure of the chi_P spectral attack family is now FACTORED into two separately-quantified sub-barriers at separate scales (21% at q≤N^{0.185} subpolynomial / 79% at q≥N^{0.185} information-theoretic), whereas before the closure was monolithic via "E2.1 + S74 → C-circular C2 collapse". **Closure mode C** (computability-circular within the C2 chain): every step of the decomposition reduces to a known barrier; no polylog short-cut. **Verification log**: this synthesis is preceded by 19 verify slots (S167, S170-S189), with substantive empirical claim (21% fraction at canonical k_*) confirmed nineteen times by independent recomputation; PARTIAL verdicts in S176/S182/S184/S185/S186/S188/S189 all about scope qualifiers (rule-dependence of k_*, post-hoc precision pinning, finite-N convergence rate) not about the substantive claim. **Thread status**: DONE — recommendation: next commit slot pick Thread 2 (Connes-Consani-Moscovici operator amortisation per CLAUDE.md priority); proposed B-grade frame-shift follow-on for non-commit rotation: Voiculescu-Speicher higher free cumulants on the bulk to test Wigner-Dyson level-spacing prediction (NOT next commit thread). Cites E2.1, E1.5, S74, S82, S148, S166, S168, S169. Cross-domain refs (compiled, all analytic NT — thread does NOT pass A-grade cross-domain criterion): Hardy-Wright Ch.16,18; Iwaniec-Kowalski §3.4; Davenport Ch.6,8,22; Tenenbaum §I.4.4-5; Wirsing 1956; Gallagher 1970; Montgomery-Vaughan Ch.9,17; Bai-Silverstein §3.3. See archive/sessions/session190_commit_s82_invariant_subspace.md. | 190 |
