eventual-period search T ≤ 200 on χ_P ≤ 200000 shows max agreement 0.88 (no period); T4 Erdős-Turán equidistribution: closest root of f_N(t) to t=1 halves as N doubles (0.093 → 0.048 → 0.023 → 0.012 → 0.006 for N ∈ {64, 128, 256, 512, 1024}) — confirms NO stable Pemantle-Wilson critical point exists; T5 sanity test on diagonal sequence π(n) at degree ≤ 6. **Adds EDGE E7.21**: Pólya-Carlson natural-boundary barrier rules out the entire ACSV smooth-point technique class, plus Wilf-Zeilberger creative-telescoping, holonomic-gradient, and Karr-Schneider Π Σ-symbolic summation methods (each requires D-finite input). Distinct from E2.20 Mahler / E2.21 Newman (which measure specific extremal values of f_N on archimedean |z|=1; E7.21 is a structural statement about the limit f). Strict strengthening of CLOSED row 584 (empirical low-order → unconditional all-order). **Cross-domain ingredient**: ACSV §7 PROPOSED → USED I; the actual technical content is the meta-fact that ACSV-class techniques require D-finite input + the rigorous combination Pólya-Carlson + Skolem-Mahler-Lech + finite-singularity D-finite theorem + Furstenberg-Lipshitz. **Falsifier**: exhibit any (a) polynomial-coefficient linear recurrence on χ_P valid for large n, OR (b) polynomial Q(z, w) ∈ ℚ[z, w] with Q(z, f(z)) = 0, OR (c) multivariate rational F(z_1, ..., z_d) and direction r ∈ ℤ_{>0}^d such that [z_1^{r_1 n} ⋯ z_d^{r_d n}] F = χ_P(n) for large n. Each is impossible by the theorem; anyone exhibiting one resolves the polylog π(x) problem. **Channelled mathematician**: Pemantle / Flajolet (combinatorial asymptotics) — the actual lever is the meta-result. **Successors proposed (S197)**: D32.a (transcendental-F Pemantle-Wilson — does a non-algebraic but holonomic-D-module F escape Lipshitz?, 1 session); D32.b (Schur-class non-rational generating-function expansions; orthogonal to the rational class, may admit different asymptotic machinery, 2 sessions). Cross-domain refs: Pólya 1916 *Sitzungsber. Berlin Math. Ges.*; Carlson 1921 *Math. Z.* 9, 1; Skolem 1934 / Mahler 1935 / Lech 1953; Furstenberg 1967 *J. Algebra* 7, 271; Lipshitz 1988 *J. Algebra* 113, 373; Stanley 1999 *EC2* CUP Thm 6.4.6; Flajolet-Sedgewick 2009 *AC* Thm B.13; Erdős-Turán 1950 *Ann. Math.* 51 (root equidistribution); Pemantle-Wilson 2013/2024 *ACSV* CUP. See `experiments/constructions/acsv_pi_diagonal/`, `archive/sessions/session197_wild_swing_acsv_d32.md`. | 197 |
